ics of fluctuations in time crystals"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Castillo, E."},{"full_name":"Koch, B."},{"full_name":"Palma, G."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321401"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1411.4236","label":"21","misc":["Semiclassical time crystal in the chiral GrossNeveu model"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Thies, M."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1328518"}},{"reference":{"label":"22","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"98","artid":"491","year":2013,"page_start":"491","journal_title":"JETP Lett."},"misc":["On the Broken Time Translation Symmetry in Macroscopic Systems: Precessing States and OffDiagonal Long-Range Order"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Volovik, G."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1253379"}}],"number_of_pages":5,"legacy_creation_date":"2014-10-09","preprint_date":"2014-10-08","author_count":2,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"5 pages, 1 figure; v3: A typo is corrected; the version to appear in Phys. Rev. Lett"}],"earliest_date":"2014-10-08","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"3458373"},{"schema":"ADS","value":"2015PhRvL.114y1603W"}],"facet_author_name":["2721575_Masaki Oshikawa","1259371_Haruki Watanabe"],"core":true,"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"},{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1321015","updated":"2025-10-03T07:48:45.880564"},"journal_title_variants":["Phys. Rev. Lett.","Phys.Rev.Lett."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["cond-mat.stat-mech","cond-mat.other","hep-th","math-ph","math.MP","quant-ph"],"value":"1410.2143"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["S.Tsuchiya.1","Peng.Zhang.4","Li.Min.Duan.1","G.Marmorini.1","G.E.Volovik.1","E.Castillo.2","Z.X.Gong.1","G.A.Palma.1","Patrick.Bruno.1","H.T.Quan.1","H.Hayakawa.2","X.Zhang.85","A.Nicolis.1","R.Yoshii.2","B.Koch.1","M.Thies.1","M.Nitta.1","Federico.Piazza.1","Tong.Cang.Li.1","L.M.Duan.1","Z.q.Yin.1","H.X.Yin.1","S.Takada.5","Frank.A.Wilczek.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"fig1.png","material":"preprint","caption":"Time-dependent correlation. (a) Wigner crystal of ions in a ring threaded by an Aharonov-Bohm flux, as proposed in Ref.~\\cite{TongcangLi} as a possible realization of a time crystal. (b) Illustration of the time dependent correlation function, should the time crystal is indeed realized as a spontaneous rotation of the density wave (crystal) in the ground state, as proposed. The density-density correlation function between $(x_1,t_1)$ and $(x_2,t_2)$ must exhibit an oscillatory behavior as a function of $t_1-t_2$ for fixed $x_1$ and $x_2$.","label":"fig1","source":"arxiv","key":"e1dddf4865539aa1813aadea226e77ba","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e1dddf4865539aa1813aadea226e77ba"}],"legacy_version":"20180607212556.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Theory-HEP"},{"term":"General Physics"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics"},{"term":"Quantum Physics","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Condensed Matter","source":"arxiv"}],"first_author":{"emails":["hwatanabe@berkeley.edu"],"full_name":"Watanabe, Haruki","last_name":"Watanabe","first_name":"Haruki","recid":1259371},"control_number":1321015,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRevLett.114.251603"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1103/PhysRevLett.114.251603"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Watanabe:2014hea"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"In analogy with crystalline solids around us, Wilczek recently proposed the idea of “time crystals” as phases that spontaneously break the continuous time translation into a discrete subgroup. The proposal stimulated further studies and vigorous debates whether it can be realized in a physical system. However, a precise definition of the time crystal is needed to resolve the issue. Here we first present a definition of time crystals based on the time-dependent correlation functions of the order parameter. We then prove a no-go theorem that rules out the possibility of time crystals defined as such, in the ground state or in the canonical ensemble of a general Hamiltonian, which consists of not-too-long-range interactions.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"In analogy with crystalline solids around us, Wilczek recently proposed the idea of \"time crystals\" as phases that spontaneously break the continuous time translation into a discrete subgroup. The proposal stimulated further studies and vigorous debates whether it can be realized in a physical system. However, a precise definition of the time crystal is needed to resolve the issue. Here we first present a definition of time crystals based on the time-dependent correlation functions of the order parameter. We then prove a no-go theorem that rules out the possibility of time crystals defined as such, in the ground state or in the canonical ensemble of a general Hamiltonian, which consists of not-too-long-range interactions.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["cond-mat.stat-mech"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Absence of Quantum Time Crystals"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Absence of Quantum Time Crystals in Ground States"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2015-06-24"}],"curated":true},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1321015?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1321015"},"created":"2014-10-09T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2025-10-03T07:48:45.880564+00:00","id":"1321015"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Watanabe%3A2014hea&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}